      <p>To say what you <b>would like</b> to do — softer and more polite than <span class="es">quiero</span> — use <span class="es">gustaría</span> + an <b>infinitive</b>. Same pronouns as <span class="es">gustar</span>:</p>
      <div class="eqn"><span class="es">me gustaría</span> + infinitive<small>me / te / le / nos / os / les gustaría + inf = I / you / … would like to…</small></div>
      <ul>
        <li><span class="hl v">Me gustaría</span> viajar a España. — I <b>would like</b> to travel to Spain.</li>
        <li><span class="hl v">Nos gustaría</span> visitar el museo. — We <b>would like</b> to visit the museum.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Also polite:</b> <span class="es">quisiera</span> + infinitive = "I would like" (<span class="es">quisiera reservar una mesa</span>). These are <b>fixed polite forms</b> — the full conditional tense comes in cluster 7.</p>
